      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part III response or note to any other line in Part III</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>PART III LINE 28 EXEMPT PURPOSE ACHIEVEMENTS:IN OCTOBER 2023, THE ELEMENTARY SCHOOL CONDUCTED A JOG A THON WITH THE SUPPORT OF STAFF AND PARENT VOLUNTEERS. $17,918.77 WAS RAISED. FOUNDATIONS FUNDS PAY FOR FIELD TRIPS AND FAMILY EVENTS. FIELD TRIPS INCLUDE MOUNTAIN VALLEY RANCH PUMPKIN PATCH (KINDER), SAN DIEGO CHILDREN DISCOVERY MUSEUM (TRANSITIONAL KINDERGARTEN), OLIVEWOOD GARDENS (SECOND GRADE), ZOO BUS TOUR (SECOND AND FOURTH GRADE) AND BOOMERS (FIFTH GRADE). $5,955.11 WAS SPENT ON ADMISSIONS AND PARKING FOR FIELD TRIPS. FAMILY EVENTS INCLUDE FAMILY BBQ DAY, FAMILY MOVIE NIGHT, LITERACY NIGHT, AND STEAM NIGHT. $7.143 WAS SPENT ON THESE EVENTS. PART III LINE 29 EXEMPT PURPOSE ACHIEVEMENTS:THE MIDDLE SCHOOL RAISED $5,841 THROUGH SNACK BAR SALES. IN THE FALL AND SPRING FALCON DAYS (FALCON IS THE SCHOOL MASCOT) WERE HELD, AN AFTER-SCHOOL EVENT. IT OFFERS A DANCE, SPORTS GAMES, ART ROOMS, AND A MOVIE OPTION FOR KIDS. IT ALLOWS MORE KIDS TO PARTICIPATE SINCE NOT EVERYONE WANTS TO GO TO THE DANCE. THE FOUNDATION PROVIDED $815 FOR STAFF MEALS OR REFRESHMENTS DURING STAFF MEETINGS. PART III: LINE 30 EXEMPT PURPOSE ACHIEVEMENTS:WINTER FESTIVAL IS A NEW EVENT STARTING WINTERDECEMBER 20, 2023, IT IS DURING SCHOOL HOURS. THE QUAD WAS DECORATED FOR A WINTER THEMED FESTIVAL. THERE WERE GAMES WITH PRIZES, CANDY HANDED OUT, THE MUSIC DEPARTMENT WILL HAVE PERFORMANCES, AND DECORATED PHOTO OPS.</ExplanationTxt>
